al and Molecular Microbiology, Structural Biology Research Center, VIB, Brussels, Belgium</aff><aff id="aff4"><label>d</label>Structural Biology Brussels, Vrije Universiteit Brussel, Brussels, Belgium</aff></contrib-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="editor"><name name-style="western"><surname>Dermody</surname><given-names initials="TS">T. S.</given-names></name><role>Editor</role></contrib></contrib-group><author-notes><corresp id="cor1">Address correspondence to Xavier Saelens, <email>xavier.saelens@vib-ugent.be</email>.</corresp><fn id="fn1" fn-type="present-address"><label>*</label><p>Present address: Mogam Biotechnology Institute, Yongin-si, Gyeonggi-do, Republic of Korea.</p></fn><fn fn-type="other"><p><bold>Citation</bold> Cho KJ, Schepens B, Moonens K, Deng L, Fiers W, Remaut H, Saelens X. 2016. Crystal structure of the conserved amino terminus of the extracellular domain of matrix protein 2 of influenza A virus gripped by an antibody. J Virol 90:611–615. doi:<ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/10.1128/JVI.02105-15">10.1128/JVI.02105-15</ext-link>.</p></fn></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="epreprint"><day>14</day><month>10</month><year>2015</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="collection"><day>1</day><month>1</month><year>2016</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>17</day><month>12</month><year>2015</year></pub-date><volume>90</volume><issue>1</issue><issue-id pub-id-type="pmc-issue-id">262938</issue-id><fpage>611</fpage><lpage>615</lpage><history><date date-type="received"><day>8</day><month>9</month><year>2015</year></date><date date-type="accepted"><day>8</day><month>10</month><year>2015</year></date></history><pub-history><event event-type="pmc-release"><date><day>17</day><month>06</month><year>2016</year></date></event><event event-type="pmc-live"><date><day>17</day><month>06</month><year>2016</year></date></event><event event-type="pmc-last-change"><date iso-8601-date="2020-12-13 19:16:25.140"><day>13</day><month>12</month><year>2020</year></date></event></pub-history><permissions><copyright-statement>Copyright © 2015, American Society for Microbiology. All Rights Reserved.</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2015</copyright-year><copyright-holder>American Society for Microbiology</copyright-holder></permissions><self-uri xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" content-type="pmc-pdf" xlink:href="zjv611.pdf"/><self-uri xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" content-type="pdf" xlink:href="zjv00116000611.pdf"/><abstract><p>We report the crystal structure of the M2 ectodomain (M2e) in complex with a monoclonal antibody that binds the amino terminus of M2. M2e extends into the antibody binding site to form an N-terminal β-turn near the bottom of the paratope. This M2e folding differs significantly from that of M2e in complex with an antibody that binds another part of M2e. This suggests that M2e can adopt at least two conformations that can elicit protective antibodies.</p></abstract><funding-group><award-group id="award1"><funding-source id="gs1">IUAP</funding-source><award-id rid="gs1">BELVIR project p7/45</award-id><principal-award-recipient>Xavier Saelens</principal-award-recipient><principal-award-recipient>Lei Deng</principal-award-recipient></award-group><award-group id="award2"><funding-source id="gs2">Ghent University BOF</funding-source><award-id rid="gs2">BOF12/GOA/014</award-id><principal-award-recipient>Xavier Saelens</principal-award-recipient><principal-award-recipient>Bert Schepens</principal-award-recipient></award-group><award-group id="award3"><funding-source id="gs3">China Scholarship Council (CSC)
